  "decision_target_date": "03/11/2025",
  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - By reason of combined back garden siting, scheme layout, design, height, bulk and massing the proposed development results in an unsympathetic, ambiguous, incongruous and cramped form of overdevelopment that fails to reflect typical backgarden structures in the locality.  The scheme is therefore in conflict with, in particular, Policies D1, D3 and D4 of the London Plan 2021, Policies D12.2 and D12.5 of Merton Local Plan (2024) and the NPPF.",
    "Reason : 2 - By reason of absence of satisfactory replacement tree planting, the scheme would have adversely impact on the ecological and biodiversity value of the borough and would fail to safeguard the visual amenity of the locality. This proposal would not ensure landscape features are protected therefore undermining the London Borough of Merton's efforts to conserve and enhance the natural environment contrary to, in particular, Chapter 15 of the NPPF 2023, London Plan Policy G7, Policy CS13 of the Core Planning Strategy 2011 and Policy D12.3 and O15.5 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 3 - By reason of combined siting, layout, access, design and the intensification of use of the shared side passage the scheme is considered to result in an unsympathetic form of development that would result in noise and disturbance and unacceptable overlooking, perceived overlooking and loss of privacy to nearby occupants failing to accord with the aims and objectives of, in particular, Policy D12.3 of Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 4 - By reason of unsatisfactory layout and access to the bike store, the scheme fails to promote sustainable form of travel, contrary to the aims and objectives set out in, in particular, London Plan Policies T5 and T6.1 and Merton Core Strategy (2011) Policy CS18.",
    "Reason : 5 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure an appropriate contribution towards offsite affordable housing or a satisfactory financial viability assessment to justify the lack of, the scheme fails to address the recognised housing need and will be contrary to, in particular, Policy H11.1 of Merton's Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 6 - By reason of absence of a legal agreement to secure the required carbon offset fund the scheme fails to provide a sustainable and energy efficient scheme contrary to the aims and objectives of, in particular, policy CC2.2 of Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 7 - By reason of absence of a legal agreement securing the self-build status of the development, the scheme fails to comply with requirements set out in, in particular, the Environment Act 2021, The Biodiversity Gain Requirements (Exemptions) Regulations 2024 and Merton Local Plan Policy O15.3.",
    "Reason : 8 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did engage in pre-application discussions but the advice was not followed.\r\n"
  ],
